WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.970
It was an era when a man lived as a warrior...

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.780
He fought, staking his life on
his faith in the sword...

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.610
The final era... the Bakumatsu.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.000
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.850
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.690
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:57.900
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.570
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.170
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:12.240
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:19.250
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.350
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:36.270
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.780
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.050
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:20.270
So it's finally started moving!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.510
It's finally begun!

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:48.940
Shinta, it's gotten to my brain...
This is not good...

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.500
This is not good...

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.550
Where am I?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.490
I've decided!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.360
I've decided, Oryo!

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:18.030
I will make a "company"!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.640
You're rushing it.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:29.610
Ryo!

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.350
It's not daybreak yet...

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.520
Ryo...

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.590
Ryo!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.060
I won't let you get away!

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.440
What are you doing?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.940
That's exactly what we want to ask you.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.610
First of all, what are you doing in Yokohama?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.410
Would you please tell us?

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.070
Akizuki-sama.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.150
I'm not obligated to tell you anything.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.680
We lost our enemy because of you!

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.260
If only you weren't there!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.970
So now you owe us one.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.370
Master.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.780
Right now it's more important
to find the man we lost.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:43.420
There has to be someone in the
Underground Auction connected to the man.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.390
You're right. If we track that person...

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.830
Yojiro Akizuki? Who is that?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.730
T.B. Glover

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:58.800
I have my people looking into it
right now, Mr. Glover.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:05.940
At any rate, he's contributed to
increasing the value of "that thing".

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.570
I see. I guess you need to thank him for that.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.060
Where are you going, Hario-dono?

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:38.840
I thought Nakaiya assigned you
to guard this Gatling gun for us

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.510
since we're not very familiar with Yokohama...

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:47.480
But it seems that the only thing
you're interested in

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.490
is the man who struck apart
the Head of the Conqueror.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:58.300
We weren't going to rely on that anyway.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.630
So it's come to this...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.460
Then don't get in my way.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.870
I'm the one who's going to kill him.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.660
Wait!

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.100
How dare you?

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.340
Wait!

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.640
It's no time to be arguing right now!

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.050
There are many, including both
the Imperial and Shogunate forces,

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.540
who are plotting to steal
this latest weapon from us.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.390
So what's most important right now
is to evade them all

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.760
and safely transport it from
Yokohama to Nagaoka Province.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.890
This will be extremely difficult.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.560
Where is he?

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.410
Why are you following me?

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:28.850
Why indeed...

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:36.960
Actually it doesn't even matter why.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.330
I just want to kill you. That's all.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.770
The Earth-splitting Sword.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.010
A powerful sword style whose forms
incorporate sword techniques

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.340
developed during the Two Imperial Courts
and the Warring States eras.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:57.680
It slices an armored enemy
in half in a single stroke.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:09.980
After more than 200 years of peace, there
can't be many users with that level of skill today.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.650
That could be another clue to find him, too.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.860
Earth-splitting, huh...

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.280
Then...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:44.980
I'll use Water!

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.190
I knew it!

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.060
Damn.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:00.980
That was careless of me...

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.550
What?

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.320
THAT Akizuki?

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.060
Right.

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:14.050
Supposedly he's the one
who murdered Ryoma Sakamoto.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.460
Murdered...

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:16.220
Yup.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:21.090
They say he was held for two months
in prison for questioning.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:22.560
Are you sure about that?

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:26.540
He didn't look like a bad person to me.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:29.010
It's from a credible source.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.850
Let's just say I met with my old buddies
when I was doing some research on that guy.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.410
That subject happened to come up.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.750
It's information from a guy who knows
people in the government.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:42.720
But they eventually released him, which means...

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:46.620
Well, you know he might've been innocent,

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:52.390
but still he was the first one to be accused
by the Shinsengumi and the patrolmen.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.860
He must've been somehow
connected to the man.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.900
It's a surprise at any rate...

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:02.410
Don't tell me...

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.200
...you knew about it?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.070
Master!

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:10.110
I've got some information on him.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:16.480
He's Genba Hario, hired as a bodyguard for
Lord Tsuginosue Kawai of Nagaoka Province.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.650
Nagaoka Province?

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.620
It sounds like he was sent by
the owner of the Auction.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.260
Something doesn't smell right...

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.070
I also confirmed the fact he's
the user of that sword technique.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:28.960
This time for sure...

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.700
I knew you would be showing up by now.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.860
Akizuki-sama!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.810
What brought you here?

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:43.310
So now you want to work as a bodyguard?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.980
I quit doing such things already.

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:49.350
I'm just here to pay my debt to you. That's all.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:52.960
And you expect us to trust you?

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.250
I don't want to work with him!

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.190
I'll ask you to do it.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.090
It's better to have more people.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.790
What do you say, Leader?

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.100
Well, as long as Akizuki-sama is okay with it.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.820
Hey, you sure this is the right way?

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.830
Yeah. Supposedly he's going to take this path.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:07.230
That's the Master's reading.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.790
Akizuki-sama. Akizuki-sama...

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.660
Don't talk!

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.780
What kind of man is Hario?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.640
I-I'm sorry about that.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:27.210
I guess it's been about 10 years.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.690
It happened in the large store
in the western province.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.230
Father!

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:45.800
I'm back.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.200
Here's your souvenir.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:56.100
It's the same thing. You can have it, too.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.150
It's for me?

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:04.290
He was a shipping agent,
a supporter of the Imperial cause.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.490
That may have been the reason why...

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:23.100
We became one of the unnamed victims
of the so-called "Ansei Purges".

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:26.010
That's the daughter, huh?

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:29.740
I must kill every one of you.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.840
Lady!

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.320
You little worm!

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:10.820
We lost everything and wandered
around all over the place...

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:16.220
One thing led to another,
and we became a performance troupe.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:24.060
Seasons may have passed,

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:29.300
but the flames of revenge burning
inside us are only growing.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:33.940
Genba Hario... That man is our enemy.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.070
Who are they?

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.270
Wh-what do you think you're doing?

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.280
How dare you!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.490
Wait.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:00.490
I believe you have an important duty
to carry out, Kawai-sama.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:03.060
Who are you?

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:05.760
Kawai-sama!

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.610
They may be from the
Kanagawa Magistrate's Office!

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:11.080
I guess this is it.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.340
Come this way.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:29.990
What?

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.860
Why you... The water, huh...

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:45.580
The cold, painful wind blows
in this corrupt world...

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:47.840
...as I travel through the west to the east!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:57.390
As I close my eyes, I see
what happened ten years ago.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.950
That day, that night and that hour!

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:06.690
Before you, who killed and burned
my parents along with their shop,

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.730
our wish will come true as we perform our play.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:13.600
The Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe is out for revenge!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.700
We'll have you spit everything out.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.470
You're going to tell us everything!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:26.840
Revenge? That's ridiculous.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:31.210
Sorry to tell you this, but I don't remember
ever seeing any of your faces.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.340
What?

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:37.090
Imagine how many worms have been killed
by my Earth-Splitting Sword.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:40.500
I don't have time to be
remembering every one of you.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.300
H-how dare you!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.200
Then your life ends here!

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:58.570
You're not getting away!

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:08.980
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:11.280
What is your name?

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.920
It's not worth mentioning, however...

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.620
However?

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.130
If you wish to know something
to remember me by,

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:22.930
know that there was one who wished
to see this Land of Rising Sun

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.330
become one of the greatest
nations in the world.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:29.140
You wish to see this country as a true nation...

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.540
The reason Tsuginosuke Kawai
bought this Gatling gun

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:35.240
was so that Nagaoka Province could
enforce an armed neutrality

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:38.710
between the Imperial and the Shogunate forces.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.440
However, soon after these events,
the Ojiya Negotiations would break down

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:48.120
and Nagaoka Province would join the
Shogunate Forces in the Battle of Hokuetsu.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:56.470
So you came here to kill me?

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.330
You've got the same eyes.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.870
The eyes I had when I went to kill
Katsu-sensei before.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:08.210
Why don't you become my bodyguard, Akizuki?
What do you say?

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.840
What? Are you sure?

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:13.920
That's right.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:19.190
That man tried to protect
Ryoma Sakamoto, but couldn't.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:26.020
But the fate that man bears
is much more than that.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.500
What?

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.000
It's still here.

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:42.550
That thing is still here in Yokohama.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:54.520
So, it sounds like it came in handy.
I'm impressed that you handled it skillfully...

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:03.060
He's a guest of a traveling theater group.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.930
The Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe...

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.970
If I remember correctly,
the troupe's playwright is...

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.960
Sotetsu Ibaragi.

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:28.850
Cancel?

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:35.160
I'm fine if everyone is okay with it.

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.670
Oh well, no matter.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:44.780
Anyway, Master, I hope my role in this new play
fares better than the role of Ryoma Sakamoto.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.240
Of course.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.510
All right!

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.270
Let's start practice then!

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>THE EARTH-SPLITTING</i>
<i>SWORD LAUGHS</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:48.870
<i>EPISODE 3
BALLAD OF
STONE CRANE MANSION</i>

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:33.750
The Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe is here.

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:35.820
The Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe is here.

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:40.290
Our next performance is set in the
western province during the Ansei Era.

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:45.360
It's a story of a pathetic commoner who was
bombarded with governmental politics.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:48.570
There's a reverse side to everything.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:48.870
I'm afraid to tell you it's the same way
with the politics of society.

00:23:48.870 --> 00:24:02.570
<i>BALLAD OF</i>
<i>STONE CRANE MANSION</i>

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:52.800
I'm afraid to tell you it's the same way
with the politics of society.

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:54.470
It's our new play!

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:56.010
The Reverse Side of a Bribery Scandal!

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:58.610
The Hidden Secret of
the Director of Palace Upkeep!

00:23:58.610 --> 00:24:01.450
The curtain is now opening!
